.TH DREAMMACHINES 1
.SH NAME
dreammachines \- work-alikes of the systems surveyed in Nelson's Computer Lib/Dream Machines
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dreammachines/
.I name
.br
.B wmapp /Apps/!DreamMachines
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B dreammachines
programs are small, runnable work-alikes of the historical and
speculative computing systems Ted Nelson surveys in
.I "Computer Lib/Dream Machines"
(1974): a hypertext browser with two-way links, a branching-alternatives
outliner, a CAI/PLATO-style lesson engine, an algorithmic-composition and
video-synthesis demo, a minimal instruction-set computer, an ELIZA-style
conversational script, and three of the languages the book discusses
alongside them (TRAC, BASIC, and APL). None claims bit-for-bit fidelity
to any specific historical system; each captures the idea Nelson
describes well enough to run and be read.
.PP
Each program may be started as
.BI dreammachines/ name
or from the
.B !DreamMachines
pinboard folder.
.PP
.IR tutor (1),
.IR eliza (1),
and
.IR toycpu (1)
load their engine as a separate library module (the
.BR Tutor ,
.BR Eliza ,
and
.B Toycpu
interfaces) from
.BR plugin/ ,
the same command/library split
.IR danby (1)
uses; the rest are single self-contained programs.
.SS Hypertext & Outlining
.TP
.B dreammachines/hyperdoc
Two-way hypertext browser over the man pages, with clickable links and a
persistent link store.
See
.IR hyperdoc (1).
.TP
.B dreammachines/thinkertoy
Branching-alternatives tree editor with direct-manipulation drag layout.
See
.IR thinkertoy (1).
.SS Teaching & Conversation
.TP
.B dreammachines/tutor
Plain-text CAI/PLATO branching-lesson engine.
See
.IR tutor (1).
.TP
.B dreammachines/eliza
Weizenbaum's ELIZA: keyword-ranked pattern matching over a script, not a
language model.
See
.IR eliza (1).
.SS Computing & Languages
.TP
.B dreammachines/toycpu
A Little Man Computer: 100 mailboxes, one accumulator, ten instructions.
See
.IR toycpu (1).
.TP
.B dreammachines/trac
The TRAC rescan-based text-macro language.
See
.IR trac (1).
.TP
.B dreammachines/basic
A small interactive BASIC.
See
.IR basic (1).
.TP
.B dreammachines/apl
A small APL, right-to-left evaluation and literal glyph operators.
See
.IR apl (1).
.SS Media & Composition
.TP
.B dreammachines/computermovie
Keyframed 3-D camera flythrough demo.
See
.IR computermovie (1).
.TP
.B dreammachines/hypercube
A tumbling wireframe tesseract.
See
.IR hypercube (1).
.TP
.B dreammachines/videosynth
A live analog-video-synthesizer work-alike (the Sandin Image Processor).
See
.IR videosynth (1).
.TP
.B dreammachines/fantics
A scripted rhythmic-performance player (Nelson's term for the timing and
motion of the presentation itself, distinct from its content).
See
.IR fantics (1).
.SS Search
.TP
.B dreammachines/ix
TF-IDF ranked full-text search over a set of files.
See
.IR ix (1).
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /dis/dreammachines/
Compiled commands.
.TP
.B /dis/dreammachines/plugin/
Compiled Tutor, Eliza, and Toycpu library modules.
.TP
.B /lib/wmsetup
Wm menu entries.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/dreammachines
